-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9a701152a54de75617f96e4c2da262727bf9e6f98b2223f9c8e791f4c05a1d1e","event_uuid":"34bddcfa-7548-49c4-b245-094c833f4603","position":{"commit_sha":"677d7ca1fba8b780029f8559125653b655fe311d","position":"1789024783152159001-34bddcfa-7548-49c4-b245-094c833f4603"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1789024511535393001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"961d3e48-381f-460c-955f-ccdea583886c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8c04-ae95-b307-450b"},{"link_uuid":"34bddcfa-7548-49c4-b245-094c833f4603","relation":"blocks","target_id":"3e32-a859-2153-4a1b"}],"description":"## Problem\n`tests/scripts/test_feature_branch_inventory.py::test_rebased_content_equivalent_branch_reports_merged` is flaky under Linux CI. Its fake `git credential` arm emits a password and exits without consuming the credential request on stdin, while `infra/gerrit/feature-branch-inventory.sh` runs `printf ... | git credential fill` under `set -o pipefail`. If the reader exits first, the producer receives SIGPIPE and the script reports `credential fill failed`.\n\n## Evidence\n- Gerrit 2957 / CI run 34439576412 / job 102752081573 failed only this test after 20,254 passes: returncode 2, stderr `credential fill failed`, git calls `credential fill`.\n- The exact 2957 patch set passes the target test locally and changes only five unrelated comment/docstring files.\n- A fixed 10,000-run reproduction of the same small `printf | non-reading credential stub` pipeline produced 5 failures with no code changes, confirming the scheduling race.\n- Earlier bug 46be-40e8-db3f-4597 fixed a distinct inherited-BASH_ENV failure in this test; its improved diagnostics exposed this separate pipe-consumption defect.\n\n## Plan\n- Make the fake credential helper consume the complete stdin request before emitting its response, matching real `git credential fill`.\n- Add deterministic evidence that the credential path cannot fail from a writer-side SIGPIPE under the test harness.\n- Verify the focused feature-branch inventory tests under Linux/Bash and the project CI gate.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The fake credential helper consumes the credential request before returning.\n- [ ] A deterministic regression oracle covers the pipefail/SIGPIPE failure class.\n- [ ] The focused feature-branch inventory tests pass under the CI shell environment.\n- [ ] Gerrit LLM-Review and Verified pass before merge.\n\n## Scope note\nThis behavioral test-harness fix is intentionally excluded from the active comments/documentation-only epic.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/scripts/test_feature_branch_inventory.py","reason":"Make the fake git credential helper consume stdin and add a deterministic regression oracle."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["blocks","3e32-a859-2153-4a1b"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["ci","flaky-test","feature-branch"],"ticket_id":"c65c-931c-ee39-4e63","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Eliminate feature-inventory credential-stub SIGPIPE flake","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["80f283b6-809f-4520-b52e-8130be8118ad","8de7ee62-2fa8-4075-8011-ac55f6781f6e","961d3e48-381f-460c-955f-ccdea583886c","34bddcfa-7548-49c4-b245-094c833f4603"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1789028929378069001,"uuid":"d7067022-e7b8-4b82-968c-0f311ac8fe92"}